  TeslaSync — P4 feature view · 0206 · GasPriceSettings (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. Every key the native
  `GasPriceSettings` resolves through the facade (table "GasPriceSettings") lives here
  with its web `t(key, default)` English value. These entries fold into the app
  `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are kept in a
  per-surface table so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings without
  editing the shared catalog.

  The first group is the exact set of keys extracted from the web source
  (features/settings/components/GasPriceSettings.tsx, namespace "settings"). The second
  group backs the native chrome: the P4 leaf freshness / loading / empty / error copy,
  the mutation-failure toasts (web hook `onError` fallbacks), and the descriptive
  accessibility labels, so the Swift sources hold no English literals.

  The two field-help strings (`help.fields.settings.gasPriceAutoPoll`,
  `help.fields.settings.gasPricePollInterval`) are resolved against the app's GLOBAL
  catalog (the native analogue of the web global `t()`), not this per-surface table, so
  they are intentionally not redefined here — only their English fallback ships inline
  in `GasPriceSettings.Views.swift`.
*/

